   1100  fce6							; 0 = no M1 patch. Window: this VBL write -> PositionBallM1 reads it
   1101  fce6							; later the same VBL (staged-file pattern like Temp/BallX). Overscan
   1102  fce6							; routines (PHM/LWC/blast/laser) restage their own CollisionEndX values
   1103  fce6							; AFTER the cave read, so the alias never crosses a frame boundary.
   1104  fce6							; NOT zeroed with BandTab on strip kill — M1 is a whole-cave latch and
   1105  fce6							; convert guarantees its cell is solid/unpatched (wall) where it must hide.
   1106  fce6							; M1 strip DESTROYED (EnemyDeadMask b4, StripBlastCheck's M1 twin) →
   1107  fce6							; stage 0: PositionBallM1 skips ENAM1, the pack's b3 flag clears, and
   1108  fce6							; both overlay paths (PHM/blast) treat the strip as gone next frame.
   1109  fce6		       a5 99		      lda	RoomMetaA
